    "body": "For the #1735 worker, from SKULL. This is a note, not a claim.\n\nDraft PR #1756 (#1727, head 52e4c70c) adds `crates/app/src/operation/boundary_chains.rs`. It groups open edge runs into separate chains, keeps the side of each chain that holds the operation's area, refuses chains that touch or cross and an even tie by name, and runs the open ends on to the stock. It also removes the old \"picks spell N separate open runs\" refusal from the **open boundary** path (`boundary::resolve`).\n\n#1735 is about the **source selection** path (`selection.rs`, `selection_geometry_in`), so the two shouldn't collide. Reusing the chain grouping may save work, and a trial merge against `mkinney:issue/1727-boundary-edges` would show any overlap early.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
